{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"\u6d88\u8cbb\u7a0e\u306e\u7a0e\u7387\uff08\u65e5\u4ed8\u3068\u533a\u5206\u3067\u30fb\u98df\u6599\u54c1 1% \u306e\u6cd5\u6848\u306e\u5370\u3064\u304d\uff09"},"description":"Look up the Japanese consumption tax rate (\u6d88\u8cbb\u7a0e\u7387) that applies on a given date (as_of = the date of the sale) for a category the caller chooses: standard (10%: dining out \u5916\u98df, alcohol \u9152\u985e and most goods), reduced_food (8% reduced rate for food and drinks \u98f2\u98df\u6599\u54c1) or newspaper (8% for subscription newspapers issued twice a week or more). It answers with the rate under the law now in force, its national/local split, and a separate pending_change for the proposed 1% food rate for sales from 2027-04-01 to 2029-03-31 (\u6d88\u8cbb\u7a0e 1% \u3044\u3064\u304b\u3089) \u2014 that cut is still a bill in the Diet (it had not been enacted when checked on 2026-11-21), so it is marked rule_status bill and answer_is_final false, never as the confirmed rate. Use it for questions such as 'what is the consumption tax rate on date X'. Dates from 2019-10-01 to 2031-12-31.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"as_of":{"description":"\u53d6\u5f15\uff08\u8b72\u6e21\uff09\u306e\u65e5 YYYY-MM-DD\u3002\u7701\u304f\u3068\u4eca\u65e5\uff08\u65e5\u672c\u6642\u9593\uff09","maxLength":10,"type":"string"},"category":{"description":"standard\uff1d\u6a19\u6e96\u7a0e\u7387\uff08\u5916\u98df\u30fb\u9152\u985e\u30fb\u307b\u3068\u3093\u3069\u306e\u7269\uff09\u3001reduced_food\uff1d\u8efd\u6e1b\u7a0e\u7387\u306e\u98f2\u98df\u6599\u54c1\u3001newspaper\uff1d\u90312\u56de\u4ee5\u4e0a\u767a\u884c\u306e\u65b0\u805e\u306e\u5b9a\u671f\u8cfc\u8aad\u3002\u3069\u308c\u306b\u3042\u305f\u308b\u304b\u306f\u547c\u3076\u5074\uff08\u5229\u7528\u8005\uff09\u304c\u9078\u3076","enum":["standard","reduced_food","